{
  "reportDate": "2026-11-13",
  "scope": "Certified cold deletion of reviewed senses, with retained Card/Note memory and history",
  "methodology": [
    "Release arm64 production store/archive/engine commands in a signed private native host. Synthetic state only; no real clicks or installed Dev application/data access.",
    "Each size uses one closed generated seed copied independently for each trial/cold case. The fixture generator is byte-identical to the preceding checkpoint; independently generated database bytes differ across checkpoints.",
    "Eligible seeds contain a durable certificate recorded by untimed validated creation. Cold means empty application/archive/engine caches; the OS disk cache is not purged.",
    "Setup, repository construction/index installation, fixture copying, assertions and frame painting are outside timers. Result admission and scheduling browse invalidation are inside store timings; later page painting is not.",
    "Reviewed deletion keeps the same target IDs and production removeSense closure as the prior enrolled-fallback window. Its label now names the eligible path. Pre-timer indexed target-link/Card reads capture the retention baseline without loading a corpus or warming the archive.",
    "Reviewed deletion now requires a partial receipt, an unchanged saved Card, sourceMissing admission and all 1000 retained historical ratings. No complete-store warm-up precedes it.",
    "Missing-proof favorite deletes only the derived certificate before its timer and still requires full preparation. Full-store readiness runs on another fresh copy.",
    "Three trials for each of twelve operations at 10k/20k: 72 unique samples. Medians/minima/maxima describe these observations, not percentiles or hardware-independent guarantees.",
    "The full 43-operation inventory was not rerun. Browser visible counters belong to the primary fixture; auxiliary cold fixture state/history is checked separately.",
    "The generated workload has two senses/four examples per entry, semantic/classification data, review enrollments and 1000 ratings. Image-heavy and dense alias workloads have focused correctness tests, not large-library latency measurements."
  ],
